    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d383">

                <pb facs="0413" n="323" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg323"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/2382</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Consul at
                        Vladivostok</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-08-01T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 1, 1918,
                                6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your 65, July 29, 4 p.m. What military officers are with Horvat? This Government
                    will not fail to make clear its friendly purpose to safeguard Russian interests
                    and territory if it decides to take any action such as you suggest but is not
                    prepared at this time to support any one faction or party. The section of the
                    Russian Railway Corps at Nagasaki has been ordered to proceed to Vladivostok.
                    Under ordinary conditions they would serve with the Russian railway authorities.
                    What Russian railway authorities now operating railways from Vladivostok?
                    Answer.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
